WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.668 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Understand Oracle's percentage before using it.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.453 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Open Oracle for the

00:00:06.453 --> 00:00:07.725 line:92% position:50% size:90%
chart you are reviewing.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.211 line:92% position:50% size:90%
In this example, eight of

00:00:13.211 --> 00:00:14.836 line:92% position:50% size:90%
the nine checks pass.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:18.959 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Eight divided by nine

00:00:18.959 --> 00:00:20.739 line:92% position:50% size:90%
rounds to eighty-nine percent.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.477 line:92% position:50% size:90%
This is confluence: a count

00:00:25.477 --> 00:00:27.314 line:92% position:50% size:90%
of conditions that agree.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.618 line:92% position:50% size:90%
It is not the probability

00:00:30.618 --> 00:00:32.057 line:92% position:50% size:90%
that a trade will win.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.446 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Oracle and Aria use the same checks,

00:00:38.446 --> 00:00:41.246 line:92% position:50% size:90%
so they are not independent confirmations.

00:00:41.805 --> 00:00:44.356 line:92% position:50% size:90%
In another example, only six

00:00:44.356 --> 00:00:46.397 line:92% position:50% size:90%
of nine checks agree.

00:00:47.805 --> 00:00:50.718 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Read the reasons. Aria says

00:00:50.718 --> 00:00:53.630 line:92% position:50% size:90%
waiting, so leave Apply unused.

00:00:54.805 --> 00:00:58.011 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Tools help you prepare. Review the

00:00:58.011 --> 00:01:00.683 line:92% position:50% size:90%
evidence, and decide with care.
